          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Adelaide's prestige property market features a select group of boutique agencies and specialized luxury divisions renowned for pairing high-end architectural homes with digital-first, cinematic video marketing and modern social media execution.\n\nThe top boutique and design-led agencies best known for these capabilities include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. WHITEFOX Real Estate (Adelaide)\n* **Office Base:** King William Road, Hyde Park\n* **The Specialty:** Bold, fast-paced, lifestyle-first video and high-end modern design.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** WHITEFOX is arguably the benchmark for modern, social-first luxury real estate marketing across Australia. With dedicated in-house media and production styling, their listings feature punchy, cinematic walkthroughs, stylized photography, and heavy vertical (Reels/TikTok) video content. They frequently represent high-spec architectural new-builds, ultra-contemporary renovations, and luxury developer collaborations, treating property marketing more like an editorial fashion brand than a traditional brokerage.\n\n### 2. Williams Real Estate (WILLIAMS LUXURY)\n* **Lead Principals:** Stephanie Williams & John Williams\n* **The Specialty:** Trophy estates, designer builds, and signature cinematic tours.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** WILLIAMS LUXURY has long set the benchmark for prestige real estate in South Australia, holding multiple suburb and state auction records. They were among the earliest adopters in Adelaide of grand, emotive video campaigns featuring voice-over storytelling, drone sweeps, and evening twilight cinematography. Their social channels regularly feature multi-million dollar architectural masterpieces, bespoke hills retreats, and prestigious Eastern suburbs villas.\n\n### 3. Giordano & Partners Luxury Real Estate\n* **Office Base:** Pulteney Street, Adelaide\n* **The Specialty:** Low-volume, high-touch architectural masterpieces and historic retreats.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Operating strictly at the top end of the market, Giordano & Partners focuses on curated, low-volume listings. Their marketing feels like a luxury lifestyle and art publication. Video campaigns here are slower, moody, and architectural-centric—focusing on raw materials, bespoke joinery, light play, and design provenance. If a home was created by an acclaimed architect or interior designer, their social content is specifically tailored to spotlight those details.\n\n### 4. TOOP+TOOP (Prestige Division)\n* **The Specialty:** Tech innovation, in-house studio production, and architectural pedigree.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** While larger than a single-office boutique, TOOP+TOOP operates specialized prestige pods and has historically driven real estate digital innovation in SA (pioneering their own media arm, TOOP.TV). They excel at pairing YouTube Shorts, Reels, and 4K architectural films with data-driven social targeting. Their prestige team frequently lists architect-designed mid-century modern homes and contemporary builds, providing deep technical context on the architecture within their video tours.\n\n### 5. Specialized Boutique Arms at Harris Real Estate & Ouwens Casserly (OC)\n* **The Specialty:** High-reach social media infrastructure, agent-led video tours, and designer flips/builds.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** While both are prominent independent brands in South Australia, several of their top-tier luxury agents run self-contained, boutique-style teams with dedicated content creators. Agencies like Harris and OC have expansive social footprints and produce high-engagement, agent-guided walk-and-talk video reels highlighting architectural features, poolside living, and designer kitchens.\n\n---\n\n### What to Look for in Their Campaigns:\nWhen assessing these agencies for an architectural home, look for:\n* **Vertical vs. Horizontal Strategy:** Top agencies produce a widescreen 4K film for web portals/YouTube, alongside tailored 9:16 vertical cuts for Instagram Reels and TikTok.\n* **Architectural Literacy:** Video narration and social copy that credit the architect, builder, materials, and passive design principles, rather than just listing bedroom and bathroom counts.\n* **Paid Digital Reach:** A strong organic Instagram page backed by targeted Meta/Google ad spend that pushes high-impact property films to high-net-worth audiences interstate and overseas.",
